<div id="S5.SS1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p11.1" class="ltx_p">Issues per number of lines
of code in different programming languages are shown in Table <a href="#S5.T13" title="Table 13 ‣ 5.1 Issue Detection and Attempts to Fix Code using ChatGPT ‣ 5 Detection and Correction ‣ Secure Coding with AI – From Creation to Inspection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>. From the data, we can observe that by far the safest language appears to be C#, with 2,964.8 source code lines per detection. Next comes C++, with 63.7 lines per detection, and finally C, which presents as the least secure language, with only 12.2 lines per static scanner detection. However, it should be noted that the “Total detects” here includes all detections, including those with “Info” or “Note” severity.</p>
</div>
